<p>Bolivian authorities arrested alleged Uruguayan drug trafficker Sebastián Marset in Santa Cruz de la Sierra on March 13 and quickly transferred him to US custody, bringing to a close a long regional manhunt for one of South America’s most wanted fugitives. Several outlets said Bolivian antinarcotics forces raided homes in the city before a US aircraft flew Marset out, and authorities also detained four other people in the operation. The arrest matters beyond Bolivia. Marset is wanted by the United States on money-laundering allegations, and investigators have also linked him to cocaine shipments from South America to Europe and to the 2022 killing of Paraguayan prosecutor Marcelo Pecci in Colombia. His capture also points to a new phase of security cooperation between Bolivia and the United States after years of strained antidrug ties, giving the region a notable law-enforcement breakthrough in a case that crossed several borders.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/C2z4eSDVp0DCqOyGAQaWPkylT931P2ofOLFoIhCrxr1NG_2VA_Cr8Jpl-q09w1ZMN24yjmnuRN3EApDBwylVg112WIoWu5cIFLfoWeI8lJWg2C20ANjDO_2vNihvwUdmMTfynzXqiXuTwZVYYOfHIRrybThoCgNrF_pYdNM9Qc_GamQAL8E-ukiWwacahgWQHAC0iHq1coLUKDk9KMebctvtgLfHGazYvnt7pcc27MmQSMtK-3oN98HCUscrKSisL4M' alt='Members of the Bolivian security forces arrive at the Third Air Brigade’s Task Force &#x27;Red Devils&#x27; base after the arrest of suspected Uruguayan drug kingpin Sebastian Marset, one of the US DEA’s most wanted fugitives, in Santa Cruz de la Sierra, Bolivia, March 13, 2026.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>US bounty: US authorities had offered a $2 million reward linked to Marset over alleged money laundering, and El País said he was among the DEA’s five most wanted individuals.</li><li>Arrest setting: Le Monde said authorities arrested Marset in an upscale neighborhood of Santa Cruz de la Sierra.</li><li>Manhunt’s end: MercoPress said the capture ended one of the Southern Cone’s longest and most visible manhunts.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Bolivian government: Bolivia cast the arrest as the result of a domestic security operation and moved quickly to hand Marset to US authorities after the raid in Santa Cruz. (<a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/13/bolivian-authorities-capture-drug-kingpin-sebastian-marset-in-police-raid'>Al Jazeera</a>)</li><li>United States: SCMP described the handover as part of renewed antidrug cooperation with Bolivia, with the DEA set to receive Marset immediately after Bolivian forces arrested him. (<a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3346567/cartel-boss-us-most-wanted-list-captured-bolivia-raid'>South China Morning Post</a>)</li><li>Paraguayan authorities: Paraguayan officials confirmed the arrest, underscoring their continued interest because Marset has been accused of ordering the killing of prosecutor Marcelo Pecci. (<a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/13/uruguayan-fugitive-sebastian-marset-captured-in-bolivia-and-placed-in-u.s.-custody'>MercoPress</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/mar/13/uruguayan-drug-trafficking-suspect-sebastian-marset-arrested-bolivia'>Bolivia arrests alleged drug kingpin accused of putting hit on Paraguayan prosecutor</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/americas/article/3346567/cartel-boss-us-most-wanted-list-captured-bolivia-raid'>Cartel boss on US ‘most wanted’ list captured in Bolivia raid</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/drug-kingpin-wanted-us-arrested-bolivia-american-plane/'>Latin American drug kingpin wanted by U.S. is arrested in Bolivia</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://english.elpais.com/international/2026-03-13/the-fall-of-sebastian-marset-the-uruguayan-kingpin-on-the-deas-mostwanted-list.html'>The fall of Sebastián Marset, the Uruguayan kingpin on the DEA’s most‑wanted list</a> - elpais.com</li><li><a href='https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/3/13/bolivian-authorities-capture-drug-kingpin-sebastian-marset-in-police-raid'>Bolivian authorities capture drug kingpin Sebastian Marset in police raid</a> - aljazeera.com</li><li><a href='https://www.lemonde.fr/en/international/article/2026/03/14/top-narco-trafficker-marset-handed-over-to-us-after-bolivia-arrest_6751425_4.html'>Top narco trafficker Marset handed over to US after Bolivia arrest</a> - lemonde.fr</li><li><a href='https://en.mercopress.com/2026/03/13/uruguayan-fugitive-sebastian-marset-captured-in-bolivia-and-placed-in-u.s.-custody'>Uruguayan fugitive Sebastián Marset captured in Bolivia and placed in U.S. custody</a> - mercopress.com</li><li><a href='https://www.france24.com/en/live-news/20260313-top-latin-american-narco-trafficker-marset-arrested-in-bolivia-govt-source'>Bolivian authorities arrest suspected Uruguayan drug cartel leader Sebastián Marset during a police operation in Santa Cruz de la Sierra. Marset, who is wanted by several countries and has a US$2 million reward linked to money laundering allegations, is detained along with four other individuals.</a> - france24.com</li></ul>